	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4826,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4826,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4826:
	.ascii	"A SHACL-SPARQL constraint (sh:sparql) has no closed-world JSON Schema equivalent and is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4826, 96

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4827,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4827,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4827:
	.ascii	"sh:subsetOf"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4827, 11

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4828,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4828,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4828:
	.ascii	"A SHACL 1.2 sh:subsetOf constraint requires every value to be among the nodes a property path reaches from the focus node; JSON Schema constrains each property on its own and cannot relate one property's values to another path's, so the constraint is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4828, 259

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4829,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4829,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4829:
	.ascii	"sh:targetNode"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4829, 13

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4830,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4830,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4830:
	.ascii	"A shape targeted only via sh:targetNode selects specific focus nodes (a constant, or the output nodes of a node expression), not a class extension; it has no closed-world JSON Schema $def and its constraints are not enforced by the emitted schema."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4830, 247

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4831,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4831,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4831:
	.ascii	"sh:targetObjectsOf"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4831, 18

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4832,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4832,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4832:
	.ascii	"A shape targeted only via sh:targetObjectsOf selects focus nodes by a predicate's object position, not a class extension; no closed-world JSON Schema $def can be keyed and its constraints are not enforced."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4832, 205

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4833,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4833,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4833:
	.ascii	"sh:targetSubjectsOf"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4833, 19

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4834,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4834,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4834:
	.ascii	"A shape targeted only via sh:targetSubjectsOf selects focus nodes by a predicate's subject position, not a class extension; no closed-world JSON Schema $def can be keyed and its constraints are not enforced."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4834, 207

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4835,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4835,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4835:
	.ascii	"sh:targetWhere"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4835, 14

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4836,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4836,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4836:
	.ascii	"A shape targeted via sh:targetWhere selects the nodes that conform to another shape, not a class extension; it has no closed-world JSON Schema $def and its constraints are not enforced by the emitted schema."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4836, 207

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4837,@object
	.section	.rodata.cst16,"aM",@progbits,16
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4837:
	.ascii	"sh:uniqueMembers"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4837, 16

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4838,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4838,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4838:
	.ascii	"A SHACL 1.2 sh:uniqueMembers constraint (true: no repeated member; false: only a list) judges a list value node or focus node (as uniqueItems); the instance projection carries a list JSON-LD 1.1 converts (Processing Algorithms and API 8.4.2) as its @list array, which the schema judges exactly; a list it keeps as linked @graph nodes (a cell with another property, referenced twice, or an IRI) is a node reference whose members hang off other @graph nodes, and a JSON Schema keyword judges only the instance location it applies to and those beneath it ($ref resolves schemas, never instance values), so for such a value the constraint is not checked. On a node shape the focus node's own member (its rdf:first) is not compared with the members of its rdf:rest, two instance locations no JSON Schema keyword relates."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4838, 815

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4839,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4839,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4839:
	.ascii	"sh:uniqueValuesFor"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4839, 18

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4840,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4840,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4840:
	.ascii	"A SHACL 1.2 sh:uniqueValuesFor constraint forbids two target nodes of a shape from having exactly the same values for the listed properties; a JSON Schema judges one instance alone (uniqueItems is uniqueness within one array, not across instances), so the constraint is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4840, 278

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4841,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4841,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4841:
	.ascii	"sh:values"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4841, 9

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4842,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4842,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4842:
	.ascii	"A SHACL 1.2 property shape with sh:values takes the output nodes of a node expression evaluated at validation as value nodes, which a JSON document does not carry; projecting its constraints onto the document's own values would require what a computed value supplies, so the property shape is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4842, 301

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4843,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4843,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4843:
	.ascii	"sh:defaultValue"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4843, 15

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4844,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4844,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4844:
	.ascii	"A SHACL 1.2 property shape with sh:defaultValue takes the output nodes of a node expression as its value nodes when the property has no other value; a JSON document does not carry them, and projecting the shape's constraints onto the document's own values would require what the default supplies, so the property shape is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4844, 330

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4845,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4845,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4845:
	.ascii	"sh:and"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4845, 6

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4846,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4846,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4846:
	.ascii	"A sh:and constraint on a property shape judges each value node against shapes; a value is projected as a node reference (its own properties live on its separate @graph node) or a literal, so the value schema has nothing to judge and the constraint is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4846, 259

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4847,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4847,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4847:
	.ascii	"sh:or"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4847, 5

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4848,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4848,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4848:
	.ascii	"A sh:or constraint on a property shape judges each value node against shapes; a value is projected as a node reference (its own properties live on its separate @graph node) or a literal, so the value schema has nothing to judge and the constraint is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4848, 258

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4849,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4849,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4849:
	.ascii	"sh:xone"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4849, 7

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4850,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4850,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4850:
	.ascii	"A sh:xone constraint on a property shape judges each value node against shapes; a value is projected as a node reference (its own properties live on its separate @graph node) or a literal, so the value schema has nothing to judge and the constraint is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4850, 260

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4851,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4851,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4851:
	.ascii	"sh:node"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4851, 7

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4852,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4852,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4852:
	.ascii	"A sh:node constraint on a property shape judges each value node against a shape; a value is projected as a node reference (its own properties live on its separate @graph node) or a literal, so the value schema has nothing to judge and the constraint is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4852, 261

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4853,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4853,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4853:
	.ascii	"sh:qualifiedValueShape"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4853, 22

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4854,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4854,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4854:
	.ascii	"A sh:qualifiedValueShape constraint counts the value nodes that conform to a shape, which the value schema cannot judge from a node reference; on a node shape, where it is not well-formed, it judges the focus node itself, which an object schema describing the node's properties does not state, so the constraint is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4854, 323

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4855,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4855,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4855:
	.ascii	"sh:closed"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4855, 9

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4856,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4856,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4856:
	.ascii	"A sh:closed true constraint on a property shape limits the properties of each value node, which its node reference does not carry, so the constraint is dropped (on a node shape it is projected as additionalProperties false)."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4856, 224

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4857,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4857,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4857:
	.ascii	"sh:uniqueLang"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4857, 13

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4858,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4858,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4858:
	.ascii	"A sh:uniqueLang true constraint forbids two values sharing a language tag, which a schema constraining each value alone cannot state; on a node shape, where it is not well-formed, it judges the focus node itself, which an object schema describing the node's properties does not state, so the constraint is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4858, 314

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4859,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4859,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4859:
	.ascii	"sh:ConstraintComponent"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4859, 22

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4860,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4860,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4860:
	.ascii	"A custom SPARQL-based constraint component (named in the note) validates through a SPARQL query, which has no closed-world JSON Schema equivalent, so the constraint is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4860, 176

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4861,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4861,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4861:
	.ascii	"sh:minCount"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4861, 11

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4862,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4862,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4862:
	.ascii	"A sh:minCount constraint on a node shape or a member shape, where it is not well-formed, judges the focus node itself rather than a property's values, so the constraint is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4862, 180

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4863,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4863,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4863:
	.ascii	"sh:maxCount"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4863, 11

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4864,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4864,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4864:
	.ascii	"A sh:maxCount constraint on a node shape or a member shape, where it is not well-formed, judges the focus node itself rather than a property's values, so the constraint is dropped."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4864, 180

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4865,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4865,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4865:
	.ascii	"sh:pattern"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4865, 10

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4866,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4866,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4866:
	.ascii	"A sh:pattern constraint. The schema judges the lexical form of every projected value that carries one: a bare string, a literal object's @value, an IRI's @id (the full IRI), rdf:nil and true/false (constants judged at compile time); every flag, i included, has an exact ECMA-262 rewrite. It does not judge a canonical xsd:integer projected as a bare JSON number: pattern judges strings only, and the integers whose numerals a pattern matches (those starting with 1: 1, 10-19, 100-199, ...) are no finite union of the intervals and residue classes minimum, maximum and multipleOf state, so where the other constraints admit such an integer and no sh:in list makes the admissible integers finite, that part is not checked; and a pattern whose ECMA-262 translation exceeds the size bound is not emitted."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4866, 800

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4867,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4867,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4867:
	.ascii	"sh:minInclusive"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4867, 15

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4868,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4868,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4868:
	.ascii	"A sh:minInclusive constraint. A numeric bound compares a bare integer by minimum/maximum and a typed literal of an integer-family or decimal datatype by an order pattern on its lexical form (the forms on one side of a rational threshold are a regular language), exactly; it does not judge an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, whose lexical forms on one side of a bound are no regular language (among 0.0...01E<n> the value is at least 1 exactly when n exceeds the count of zeros, a comparison no finite automaton, and no ECMA-262 backreference, makes), unless sh:in makes those values finite. A temporal bound (xsd:dateTime, xsd:date, xsd:time) is judged exactly, by order patterns on the lexical form over the XSD timeline, the +-14:00 partial order between zoned and local values included."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4868, 790

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4869,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4869,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4869:
	.ascii	"sh:maxInclusive"
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4869, 15

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4870,@object
	.section	.rodata..Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4870,"a",@progbits
.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4870:
	.ascii	"A sh:maxInclusive constraint. A numeric bound compares a bare integer by minimum/maximum and a typed literal of an integer-family or decimal datatype by an order pattern on its lexical form (the forms on one side of a rational threshold are a regular language), exactly; it does not judge an xsd:double or xsd:float literal, whose lexical forms on one side of a bound are no regular language (among 0.0...01E<n> the value is at least 1 exactly when n exceeds the count of zeros, a comparison no finite automaton, and no ECMA-262 backreference, makes), unless sh:in makes those values finite. A temporal bound (xsd:dateTime, xsd:date, xsd:time) is judged exactly, by order patterns on the lexical form over the XSD timeline, the +-14:00 partial order between zoned and local values included."
	.size	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4870, 790

	.type	.Lanon.c57b04e44b95a713af94324763ba52bc.4871,@object
